 "curriculum": [
  "Speed, distance and time, and how they give each other",
  "Something moving in space keeps going until something pushes it",
  "A push changes motion, and a bigger push changes it faster",
  "A small change made early does more than a big one made late",
  "Rates: how fast something is used up, and how long it lasts",
  "A budget: a finite store shared between competing demands",
  "Energy moves from hot to cold, and insulation slows it down",
  "Air is a mixture, and the share of each gas has to stay in range",
  "Circuits: a break, a short, and why a battery has limits",
  "Signals take time to travel, and distance costs strength",
  "Spinning things keep spinning, and a nudge takes a while to show",
  "Reading a graph and spotting what changed at the moment it changed",
  "Repeats and averages, and what one reading is worth",
  "Deciding with a deadline that does not move",
  "What a measurement can honestly say, and what it cannot",
  "Ordering work when several things are wrong at once"
 ],
